WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:01.770
- [Narrator] Singles' Day in China

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.780
is the world's biggest shopping event.

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:07.350
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.550
- [Narrator] Think of Black Friday,

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:12.230
Cyber Monday and Amazon
Prime Day on loop for days.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:14.240
(lively music)

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.120
And now Alibaba, the
Chinese e-commerce giant

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.600
that created Singles' Day

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.520
wants to use its international
platform, AliExpress,

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:24.153
to help the event go global, from Poland.

00:00:24.153 --> 00:00:25.660
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:26.735
- [Narrator] To France.

00:00:26.735 --> 00:00:28.190
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:29.390
- [Narrator] And Brazil.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:33.240
Alibaba is competing with
other e-commerce platforms,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.520
like Amazon to capture a larger share

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.840
of the global market,

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.750
which is expected to grow
by $1.4 trillion by 2025.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.450
So to promote Singles' Day,

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.990
Alibaba has hired an army of influencers

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.520
around the world.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:48.700
- I love this color.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.520
- [Narrator] And beefed up its logistics.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.360
But it has to tackle some challenges

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.580
if it wants to take a
bite off a bigger piece

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.643
of the global e-commerce pie.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.790
One of the first things Alibaba is doing

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.468
to win over new Singles'
Day consumers abroad?

00:01:02.468 --> 00:01:04.020
Massive sales.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:09.020
- Discounts of up to 50 or
even 70% are being offered.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:12.030
So it's a very big event.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.300
- [Narrator] Vinci Zhang is
an e-commerce analysts based

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.570
in Shanghai who's been watching Alibaba

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:18.600
for the past seven years.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.830
- So the way it is doing that right now

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.330
is basically competing on pricing,

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.279
by offering cheaper prices,

00:01:25.279 --> 00:01:29.790
as well as charging less
fees for the merchants.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:32.110
- [Narrator] When foreign
customers use AliExpress,

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.330
they get direct access

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.830
to Chinese factories and merchants.

00:01:35.830 --> 00:01:38.300
The company's also
speeding up global delivery

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:41.960
during the international two-day
shopping event this year.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:43.660
It said it's increasing charter flights

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:46.030
from China to cities like Seoul and Paris

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:48.993
to 100 a week up from 80 flights.

00:01:50.591 --> 00:01:51.900
AliExpress said it's also installed

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.410
5,000 automated self-pickup lockers

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.340
across Russia, Poland, Spain and France

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.840
to help cut delivery costs

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.420
that would go to hiring fleets

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.405
of delivery trucks and drivers.

00:02:02.405 --> 00:02:04.510
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:05.790
- [Narrator] Daniela Sena is one

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:08.680
of the 400 influencers Alibaba has hired

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.620
to promote Singles' Day abroad.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:12.390
In China, live streaming is one

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.870
of the most popular ways to shop.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.570
And Sena is doing the same

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.880
but for a Brazilian audience.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.280
She says the Chinese company

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.740
is offering something better

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.553
than other shopping platforms.

00:02:23.553 --> 00:02:26.972
- I think the fact that people can see us,

00:02:26.972 --> 00:02:29.650
we touch the product, we have the feedback

00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:33.640
of other people that already
purchased the products as well.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:37.060
It gives the audience a
very personal communication.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:38.855
- [Narrator] But attracting
buyers won't be enough.

00:02:38.855 --> 00:02:41.200
- If it wants to compete with Amazon,

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.810
then I think fundamentally,

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.720
it needs to own more inventory.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.000
- [Narrator] And the bigger bulk items

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.560
could become an issue.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:50.640
Right now the company lacks the
infrastructure outside China

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.570
to support those kinds of sales.

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:55.470
- If we're talking about
big air conditioner

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:58.613
or refrigerator purchase
shipped from China,

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.310
I imagine it will be very challenging

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:03.710
for big home appliance manufacturers.

00:03:03.710 --> 00:03:06.770
They are not going to
sell directly in Europe

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:07.930
and build a warehouse.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.450
So it's up to Alibaba if they want

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:15.090
to kinda undertake that initiative.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.160
- [Narrator] Alibaba said it
has opened up its platform

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.290
to merchants in several
markets already outside

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.680
of China, and will continue to expand

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.930
while also developing warehouses overseas

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.980
to improve capacity.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:27.990
It said AliExpress is at the forefront

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:29.740
of it global strategy.

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.690
And according to brokerage
China Merchant Securities,

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.560
China's outbound e-commerce market

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:39.540
is expected to grow around
26% every year until 2025.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:42.870
Amazon did not respond
to a request for comment.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.610
So Zhang says Alibaba should stick

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:45.770
to what they're good at:

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.680
using automated warehouses,

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.280
innovative ways to live stream

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:52.440
and delivery packages to keep prices low.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:55.238
- I think that's where
Alibaba's strength lies.

00:03:55.238 --> 00:03:58.710
It's in its technology
and logistics management.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:02.000
If they are able to replicate
that success to Europe,

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.500
then maybe they can compete against Amazon

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:06.640
from a different angle,

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.750
and attract more people
to ultimately switch

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.193
to using Alibaba.

